    "description": "## Summary\n\nOps bans a Player through a button that requires a reason and sets Status to Banned. Unbanning is a manual status edit restricted to Ops/Admins — reps can't edit Player Status at all.\n\n## Context\n\nBanned is the one manual Player status — the automation in this epic (BUILD-178) never sets or clears it. The client asked for a controlled path: a **Ban button** on the Player that captures the reason, and unbanning restricted to Ops/Admins so reps can't flip statuses by hand.\n\n## Current state\n\nAccount.Ban_Reason\\__c and Account.Ban_Notesc exist, unused by any UI. Player_Status_\\_c is editable by anyone with the field on-layout — no restriction. A Referrer_Ban_Button screen flow already exists for the Referrer ban path — mirror its structure, naming, and UX (warning text, required reason, notes) for consistency.\n\n## Proposed solution\n\n1. NEW screen flow + quick action Ban Player on Account (Player record type): requires Ban_Reason\\__c (optional Ban_Notesc), sets Player_Status_\\_c = Banned. (Audit stamping via BUILD-251.)\n2. Unban = manually editing Player_Status__c on the record. Restrict field edit access to Ops/Admin profiles/permission sets — align with the WT permission set group model (confirm which PSG at grooming).\n3. Rep-facing layouts: Player_Status__c read-only.\n4. At grooming, confirm who can run the Ban action and the flow's run context: with rep edit access removed at field level, either restrict the quick action's visibility to Ops/Admin, or run the flow in system context if reps should be able to ban.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n1. Ban action requires a reason, sets Banned, audit fields stamped (via BUILD-251).\n2. Banned Players are ignored by the BUILD-253 and BUILD-254 automations (their ACs cover it; regression-check here).\n3. Rep users cannot edit Player_Status__c; Ops/Admin users can (unban path) — and a manual unban still stamps the audit fields (via BUILD-251).\n4. Ban action on an already-Banned Player is a no-op or blocked with a clear message.\n\n## Output\n\nScreen flow, quick action, and permission changes deployed in Partial SB; PSG used recorded on this ticket; requirements doc updated.",
